3 477:22-d QualifiedRenter/PurchaserAffidavitRequired.
4 I. Every person or entity who leases or acquires an ownership or controlling interest in
5 property within 10 miles of a protected facility shall file with the office of the attorney general,
6 within one business day of closing, or, in the case of a lease, within one business day of the delivery
7 of keys, access codes, or other methods of access to the premises, a notarized qualified
8 renter/purchaser affidavit signed under penalty of perjury, attesting that the person acquiring an
9 ownershiporcontrollinginterest,orleasingtheproperty:
10 (a) Is not a foreign principal or an agent of a foreign principal, as defined in this
11 subdivision;
12 (b) Hasreadandunderstandsboththeprohibitionsinthissubdivisionandthepenalties
13 forviolationsofthetermsofthissubdivision;and
14 (c) Isnotprohibitedfrompurchasingorleasingthepropertyunderthissubdivision.
15 II. Afailuretosubmitthequalifiedrenter/purchaseraffidavittotheattorneygeneral’soffice
16 does not affect the title or insurability of the title for the real property, or subject the listing,
17 brokering, closing, or leasing agent to civil or criminal liability, unless the agent has actual
18 knowledge that the transaction will result in a violation of this section so long as the agent has
19 complied with the notice requirement in RSA 477:4-i. Nothing in this paragraph shall preclude the
20 attorneygeneral'sofficefrominitiatingaforfeitureactioninaccordancewithRSA477:22-f.
21 III. Failure to submit a required affidavit under this section shall result in a $500 civil
22 penalty. Prior to an action against a natural person to impose the civil penalty, the attorney general
23 shall give notice and provide 60 days to cure the violation. No opportunity to cure shall be offered to
24 an entity in RSA 477:22-b, as knowledge of the filing requirement under this section shall be
25 imputed.
